        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: সঙ্গতি",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সঙ্গতি — sônggôti — \"financial means\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "যদি সঙ্গতি থাকত, তাহলে আমরা একটা বড় বাড়ি কিনতাম। Jôdi sônggôti thāktô, tāhôle āmrā ekṭā bôṛo bāṛi kintām. If we had the means, we would buy a big house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সঙ্গতি (sônggôti) is Sanskrit saṃgati, \"coming together, meeting\" (Monier-Williams); the sense \"what one can afford\" is Bengali's own."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
